  "honest_summary": "All 34 ai-core files are written and the pi-ai library itself compiles with 0 errors and 0 warnings from this slice (cargo check -p pi-ai: ok). Behaviour is ported 1:1 from the TypeScript: same names, constants, literals, defaults, error strings, JSON field names, absent-vs-null handling and ordering. 146 unit tests are included in this slice, but they could not be executed: the crate's test target does not build because 45 compile errors remain inside OTHER slices' #[cfg(test)] modules (providers/*.rs). No test binary ran, so 0 passed / 0 failed executed. Two deliberate Rust-level deviations, both documented in-file: (1) TS union types become String aliases + KNOWN_* const arrays; (2) Compat (the TS conditional type) uses a key-sniffing Deserialize because a serde untagged enum would always match the all-optional OpenAICompletionsCompat first. models.generated.ts is embedded as base64 JSON (32 providers / 1283 models) instead of 22884 lines of literals. Node http.createServer callbacks became a private `plumbing` module inside utils/oauth/mod.rs (not a new public API). The TypeBox dependency has no Rust counterpart: tool schemas are serde_json::Value and validation.ts is a hand-rolled JSON-Schema subset validator with the exact TS error strings."
